<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anandji Kalyanji Trust</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anandji Kalyanji Pedhi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anandji Kalyanji Trust is a Jain charitable trust based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmedabad">Ahmedabad</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, which manages many of the most important Shvetambara Jain temples and pilgrimage sites, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shatrunjaya">Shatrunjaya</a> at Palitana. In the 19th and 20th centuries it was in long legal disputes with the Thakores of Palitana over the taxes they levied on pilgrims.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anandji-kalyanji-trust.jpg" alt="Anandji Kalyanji Trust" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel VILLAFRUELA · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Udaipur-Jagdish_Temple-Shet_Anandji_Kalyanji_DFE-20131013.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
